            <title xml:id="title_95dd3c60" xml:lang="it">Sinfonia</title>
            <contributor xml:id="respStmt_520f52a6">
               <persName role="composer" xml:id="persName_ff34e684">Johann Adolph Scheibe</persName>
            </contributor>
            <history xml:id="history_51081849">
               <p xml:id="idm165">The present material consisting of instrumental parts to the Sinfonia in B flat major comprises two sets: an early transcription which was most likely produced around the middle of the eighteenth century in a script similar to that found in some of Scheibe's flute concertos, and a second in a script which belongs to the end of the eighteenth century and is probably based on the earlier original set. Originally, it was part of the repertoire played in the Akademiska kapellet of Lund; the collection was expanded by <persName xml:id="idm166" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">H.C. Engelhart</persName> during the years 1727–65 and was donated to Lund's academic music society in 1798.</p>
            </history>
